["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A bear lives by its nose. Beat the nose and you can get close; lose the wind and the bear is gone before you see it.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Ranking of black bear senses, strongest first. Nose: nasal lining about 100 times the area of a person, finds food over 1 km away. Ears: over twice as sensitive as human hearing, and hears higher sounds. Eyes: see colour and are sharp up close. Bar lengths show the order only. Beat the nose first.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Senses, strongest first</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"85.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose</text><rect x=\"76\" y=\"64\" width=\"150.0\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"232.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><text x=\"16\" y=\"137.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ears</text><rect x=\"76\" y=\"116\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"172.0\" y=\"137.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><text x=\"16\" y=\"189.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes</text><rect x=\"76\" y=\"168\" width=\"60.0\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"142.0\" y=\"189.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">100x our nose lining</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">over 2x our hearing</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">colour, sharp up close</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"222\" width=\"384\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bar lengths show rank only (Tip).</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose finds food over 1 km away (70%).</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Beat the nose first: the wind decides.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Nose first, ears second, eyes third <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The wind decides every bear hunt (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>The nose and how scent moves, thermals, the ears, the eyes, how a bear combines them, and how to beat each one.</li><li>Short version: <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind\">How a deer thinks</a> covers wind for all game; <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">wind and thermals</a> has the physics.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-02\">Chapter 2, The body</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-04\">Chapter 4, The mind</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a black bear feeds in a berry patch above you. At first the wind blows from the bear toward you, so your scent cone trails behind you, away from the bear. Then the wind swings around and your scent cone swings toward the bear. The bear lifts its head: it smells you. Check the wind before every move.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your scent rides the wind</text><g transform=\"translate(120 92) scale(1.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(250 84) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(320 110) scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(200 100)\"><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;-10\" keyTimes=\"0;0.9;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g transform=\"translate(200 250)\"><g><path d=\"M0 0 L-50 70 L50 70 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".22\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;180\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"6\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">You</text></g><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><g><path d=\"M40 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10 M360 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10\" fill=\"none\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 200 150;0 200 150;180 200 150\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g><text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind: bear to you. Good.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.6\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"140\" width=\"250\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind swung. Bear smells you.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Your scent rides the wind to the bear. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Nose lining about 100 times ours <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Finds food over 1 km away <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the nose in detail</summary><ul><li>North American Bear Center: smell is \"extremely good\", limits untested; nasal lining (mucosa) about 100 times the area of a person's <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>WildSafeBC: a bear can smell food over 1 km away <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>BearWise: the best nose in the bush, far better than a dog's (70%, via the quick lesson).</li><li>Bigger claims you will read (2,100 times a person, miles away) are not tested science (Tip: ignore them).</li><li>What this means: a bear that winds you leaves, usually without you ever knowing it was there (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of one day on a slope. The sun rises and crosses the sky. In the morning the sun warms the slope and blue arrows show air rising uphill. Near sunset the air swirls as the thermals switch. In the evening the slope cools and the arrows flow downhill. Morning: be above the deer. Evening: be below.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fdf1d6\"><animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#fdf1d6;#fffaf0;#e9dfcf\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect><g><circle r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateMotion dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" keyPoints=\"0;0.8;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M40 150 Q 200 -40 380 150\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0.5\" keyTimes=\"0;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><path d=\"M0 270 L300 90 L400 90 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"320,90 330,60 340,90\"/><polygon points=\"350,90 360,56 370,90\"/></g><g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M27.7 225.4 L68.8 200.7 M61.6 212.0 L68.8 200.7 L55.4 201.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M117.7 171.4 L158.8 146.7 M151.6 158.0 L158.8 146.7 L145.4 147.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M207.7 117.4 L248.8 92.7 M241.6 104.0 L248.8 92.7 L235.4 93.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;22.3 -13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Morning: sun warms the slope</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air rises UPHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M90 200 c 20 -30, 50 -10, 30 10 c -15 15, -30 -5, -15 -15\"/><path d=\"M200 140 c -20 -30, -50 -10, -30 10 c 15 15, 30 -5, 15 -15\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Near sunset: the switch</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air swirls, mixed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M68.8 200.7 L27.7 225.4 M41.0 224.4 L27.7 225.4 L34.9 214.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M158.8 146.7 L117.7 171.4 M131.0 170.4 L117.7 171.4 L124.9 160.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M248.8 92.7 L207.7 117.4 M221.0 116.4 L207.7 117.4 L214.9 106.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-22.3 13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Evening: slope cools</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air sinks DOWNHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"230\" width=\"200\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: be above</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: be below</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>Morning air climbs; evening air sinks. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Morning sun: air drifts uphill. Evening: downhill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Swirls at the switch hours (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: thermals for a bear hunter</summary><ul><li>Thermals: air slides up a slope as it warms in the morning and down as it cools in the evening (80%, <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">wind and thermals</a>).</li><li>Evening berry slope (Tip): set up below or beside the patch early, then expect your scent to sink toward the bottom as the light fades. Sit where the sinking air carries it away from the bear's likely path.</li><li>A creek bottom at dusk is a scent drain: cold air pours down it (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/wind-mastery\">wind mastery</a>).</li><li>Wind beats thermals when it blows hard (Tip).</li><li>Carry a puffer bottle or milkweed and check every few minutes (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 258\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Black bear senses. Nose: the best in the bush, far better than a dog. Ears: good, they hear high sounds beyond our range. Eyes: about as good as a person, with colour and good night vision. Most active at dawn and dusk, but any hour.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"258\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black bear senses</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"56\" width=\"230.0\" height=\"34\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"295.0\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"end\">best in the bush</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"134.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ears</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"112\" width=\"161.0\" height=\"34\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"236.0\" y=\"134.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">good, hear high</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"168\" width=\"138.0\" height=\"34\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">like ours, sees colour</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Most active at dawn and dusk, but any hour.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Over twice as sensitive as ours, higher range too <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Hearing works in all directions, even in brush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the ears in detail</summary><ul><li>North American Bear Center <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>: hearing \"over twice the sensitivity of human hearing\" and beyond human frequency ranges; \"the first line of defense\" because it works in all directions; in brushy forest a bear can hear farther than it can see.</li><li>Metal clicks, a zipper, a boot on dry sticks, voices: all carry (Tip).</li><li>Steady natural sounds (wind, creek, rain) cover you; a single sharp sound does not (Tip).</li><li>A bear crunching berries or ripping a log is noisy: that is your moment to move (Tip, chapter 9).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How to beat each bear sense, as tips. Nose: keep the wind in your face, crosswind at worst, never let the bear get downwind. Ears: move slowly, step while it feeds noisily; wind and creek noise help. Eyes: move only when its head is down, freeze when it looks, stay low.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">How to beat each sense</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"380\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind in your face. Crosswind at worst.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Never let it get downwind.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"126\" width=\"380\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ears</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Slow steps. Move when it feeds noisily.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind and creek noise help.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"202\" width=\"380\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Move only when its head is down.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Freeze when it looks. Stay low.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tips, from hunting educators</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sees colour, sharp up close <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Distance vision is untested <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the eyes in detail</summary><ul><li>North American Bear Center: bears \"see in color and have sharp vision close up\"; distance vision over about 180 m (200 yd) \"has not been tested\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A 2021 retina study predicts two colour channels (dichromatic) with high sharpness, like many mammals; an older behaviour study pointed the same way (70%, Heyward and others, University of Wisconsin summary).</li><li>Eyesight about as good as a person's, maybe better (70%, WildSafeBC).</li><li>Motion gives you away more than shape (Tip, hunter consensus). Move when it looks away.</li><li>Orange: most hunters wear it for safety. Bears likely see it less vividly than we do, but motion still shows (Tip).</li><li>A bear standing on its hind legs is usually trying to see and smell better, not about to charge (Tip, bear safety guidance).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>First warning</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Far</td><td>Nose, on the wind <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td><td>Leaves quietly (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>In brush</td><td>Ears <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td><td>Stops, listens, stands (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Close, open</td><td>Eyes, motion <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td><td>Stares, then leaves or huffs (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Nose confirms. A bear that only hears you may wait to smell you (Tip).</li><li>Stay downwind and it can only hear and see you (Tip).</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How to beat each bear sense, as tips. Nose: keep the wind in your face, crosswind at worst, never let the bear get downwind. Ears: move slowly, step while it feeds noisily; wind and creek noise help. Eyes: move only when its head is down, freeze when it looks, stay low.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">How to beat each sense</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"380\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind in your face. Crosswind at worst.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Never let it get downwind.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"126\" width=\"380\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ears</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Slow steps. Move when it feeds noisily.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind and creek noise help.</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"202\" width=\"380\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Move only when its head is down.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Freeze when it looks. Stay low.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tips, from hunting educators</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Wind first, then sound, then movement (Tip).</li><li>Approach from downwind or crosswind only (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the old hand's checklist</summary><ul><li>Before the stalk: wind check, then pick a route with the wind in your face or across it (Tip).</li><li>Scent: clean clothes, no food smells, no smoking, no cologne (Tip). Scent control helps, wind control decides (Tip).</li><li>Sound: soft soles, slow steps, sling off the metal, pockets empty (Tip).</li><li>Sight: stay below the skyline, move when the head is down, freeze when it looks (Tip).</li><li>If the wind swings to the bear: back out, circle, try again another day (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a black bear feeds in a berry patch above you. At first the wind blows from the bear toward you, so your scent cone trails behind you, away from the bear. Then the wind swings around and your scent cone swings toward the bear. The bear lifts its head: it smells you. Check the wind before every move.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your scent rides the wind</text><g transform=\"translate(120 92) scale(1.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(250 84) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(320 110) scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(200 100)\"><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;-10\" keyTimes=\"0;0.9;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g transform=\"translate(200 250)\"><g><path d=\"M0 0 L-50 70 L50 70 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".22\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;180\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"6\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">You</text></g><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><g><path d=\"M40 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10 M360 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10\" fill=\"none\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 200 150;0 200 150;180 200 150\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g><text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind: bear to you. Good.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.6\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"140\" width=\"250\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind swung. Bear smells you.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Your scent rides the wind to the bear. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Nose knows, ears warn, eyes confirm.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 100, 2, 1: nose lining 100x ours, hearing 2x, smells food over 1 km <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (widely taught hunting advice, opinion): \"Hunt the wind, not the bear.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Up in the morning, down at night: thermals tell your scent its flight.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 200 yards: beyond about 180 m (200 yd) nobody has tested bear eyesight <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, common hunting advice): \"Head down, you move. Head up, you are a stump.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Trusting scent spray instead of the wind.</li><li>Moving while the bear is looking.</li><li>Ignoring the evening downslope swing on a berry slope.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Next scouting trip: carry a puffer bottle and check the wind at every stop. Note when the thermal switches.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>North American Bear Center, <a href=\"https://bear.org/?p=53\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Senses and abilities</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>WildSafeBC, <a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/black-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 (70 to 75%)</li><li>University of Wisconsin Ophthalmology, <a href=\"https://www.ophth.wisc.edu/blog/2021/03/01/retinal-cone-photoreceptor-distribution-in-the-american-black-bear-ursus-americanus/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">retinal cone distribution in the American black bear</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>BearWise, via the <a href=\"#/s/black-bear\">quick lesson</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Hunt Mentor lessons: <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">wind and thermals</a>, <a href=\"#/s/wind-mastery\">wind mastery</a>, <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind\">How a deer thinks</a> (as marked there)</li><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-black-bear.md</code>.</li></ul>"]